          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A cogerm differential form is a vast generalization of the usual exterior
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+forms"} differential forms
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/absolute+differential+forms"} absolute differential forms
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi d
                    %mn 2
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d^2x
            and a commutative differential operator (at least in the case of 1-forms).
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            be a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            will be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifold"} manifold
            or a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+smooth+space"} generalized smooth space
          %p
            By a
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/curve"} curve
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            we mean a function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi c
                  %mo :
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mi ϵ
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ϵ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c:(-\epsilon,\epsilon)\to X
            for some real number
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϵ
                    %mo &gt;
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \epsilon\gt 0
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi c
                  %mo :
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mi ϵ
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ϵ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c:(-\epsilon,\epsilon)\to X
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi c
                  %mo ′
                  %mo :
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mi ϵ
                  %mo ′
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ϵ
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c':(-\epsilon',\epsilon')\to X
            have the same
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/germ"} germ
            (at 0) if there exists
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ϵ
                  %mo ″
                  %mo ≤
                  %mi min
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ϵ
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ϵ
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \epsilon'' \le min(\epsilon,\epsilon')
            such that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi c
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi c
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c'
            agree when restricted to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mi ϵ
                    %mo ″
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ϵ
                    %mo ″
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-\epsilon'',\epsilon'')
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C X
            denote the set of germs of curves in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient"} quotient
            of the set of curves in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+relation"} equivalence relation
            “has the same germ as”.
          .un_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              A (partial)
              %strong cogerm differential 1-form
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partial+function"} partial function
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ω
                      %mo :
                      %mi C
                      %mi X
                      %mo →
                      %mi ℝ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega : C X \to \mathbb{R}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
              on a curve
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
              (or germ thereof) as
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                      %mi ω
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi c
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \langle \omega | c \rangle
          %h2#examples Examples
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo :
                      %mi X
                      %mo →
                      %mi ℝ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f: X\to \mathbb{R}
                is a function, then it defines a cogerm differential 1-form, also denoted
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                = succeed ":" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi c
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi f
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi c
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \langle f | c \rangle = (f\circ c)(0).
              %p
                This is defined on
                %em all
                germs.
            %li
              %p
                We also have the differential of
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} d
                        %mi f
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{d}f
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} d
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi c
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi f
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi c
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ′
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \langle \mathrm{d}f | c \rangle = (f\circ c)'(0)
              %p
                which is defined on all germs
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi c
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
                having the property that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi c
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\circ c
                is differentiable at
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                is smooth (for
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                a
                = succeed ")," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+space"} smooth space
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} d
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{d}f
                is defined on all smooth germs.
              %p
                When
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                is a
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differentiable+manifold"} differentiable manifold
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} d
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi c
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \langle \mathrm{d}f | c \rangle
                depends only on the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+vector"} tangent vector
                of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi c
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
                at
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
            %li
              %p
                More generally, any real-valued function on the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+bundle"} tangent bundle
                of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                can be regarded as a cogerm differential 1-form; this includes in particular all
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+form"} exterior differential 1-forms
            %li
              %p
                We also have the second differential
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} d
                          %mn 2
                        %mi f
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{d}^2f
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                      %msup
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} d
                        %mn 2
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi c
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi f
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi c
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ″
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ,
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \langle \mathrm{d}^2f | c \rangle = (f\circ c)''(0),
              %p
                which depends only on the 2-
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/jet"} jet
                of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi c
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
                at
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi c
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
                may be called a
                = succeed "." do
                  %em cojet differential 1-form
            %li
              %p
                For an example of a cogerm differential form that is not a cojet differential form, let
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                      %mrow
                        %mi ω
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi c
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \langle{\omega|c}\rangle
                be
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
                or
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
                according as
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi c
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
                is or is not
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/analytic+function"} analytic
                (say for
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                the real line). We do not know any more interesting examples.
            %li
              %p
                We can also apply arbitrary real functions: if
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mo :
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi n
                      %mo →
                      %mi ℝ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi:\mathbb{R}^n\to \mathbb{R}
                is a function (or even a partial function) and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi ω
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mi …
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi ω
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega_1,\dots,\omega_n
                are cogerm differential 1-forms, then we have
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi ω
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mi …
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi ω
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi(\omega_1,\dots,\omega_n)
                defined by
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi ω
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mi …
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi ω
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi c
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                      %mo =
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                      %msub
                        %mi ω
                        %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi c
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                      %mo ,
                      %mi …
                      %mo ,
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                      %msub
                        %mi ω
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi c
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \langle \phi(\omega_1,\dots,\omega_n) | c \rangle = \phi(\langle\omega_1|c\rangle,\dots,\langle\omega_n|c\rangle)
            %li
              %p
                For instance, any
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ω
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
                has an absolute value
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mi ω
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {|\omega|}
            %li
              %p
                And if
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                        %mo =
                        %msup
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X=\mathbb{R}^2
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi đ
                        %mi s
                        %mo =
                        %msqrt
                          %mrow
                            %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} d
                            %msup
                              %mi x
                              %mn 2
                            %mo +
                            %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} d
                            %msup
                              %mi y
                              %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} &amp;#273; s = \sqrt{\mathrm{d}x^2 + \mathrm{d}y^2}
            %li
              %p
                Generalizing
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi đ
                        %mi s
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} &amp;#273;s
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/absolute+differential+form"} absolute differential 1-form
                can be regarded as a cogerm differential 1-form.
            %li
              %p
                Any
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+bilinear+form"} symmetric bilinear form
                on tangent vectors can also be regarded as a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quadratic+form"} quadratic
                covector form and therefore a quadratic cogerm form. In particular, this applies to the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemannian+metric"} metric
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi g
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
                on any (pseudo)-
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemannian+manifold"}> Riemannian manifold
                \. We then have
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi g
                      %mo =
                      %mi đ
                      %msup
                        %mi s
                        %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g = &amp;#273;s^2
                in the algebra of cogerm forms on a Riemannian manifold.
            %li
              %p
                For any function
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Δ
                        %mi f
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta f
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo +
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} d
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo −
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(x+\mathrm{d}x)-f(x)
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                is the
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Heaviside+function"} Heaviside function
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta f
                is a candidate for the
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac+delta+function"} Dirac delta function
            %li
              %p
                A somewhat better way to represent the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac+delta+function"} Dirac delta function
                as a cogerm differential form is
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi δ
                      %mo =
                      %mrow
                        %mo {
                        %mrow
                          %mtable{:columnalign => "left left", :displaystyle => "false"}
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %mfrac
                                  %mn 1
                                  %mrow
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} d
                                    %mi x
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                              %mtd
                                %mspace{:width => "2em"}
                                %mi x
                                %mo =
                                %mn 0
                                %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                                %mi and
                                %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                                %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} d
                                %mi x
                                %mo ≠
                                %mn 0
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %mn 0
                              %mtd
                                %mspace{:width => "2em"}
                                %mi otherwise
                                %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\delta =
                      \\begin{cases}
                      \\frac{1}{|\mathrm{d}x|} &amp;\qquad x=0 \;and\; \mathrm{d}x\neq 0\\
                      0 &amp;\qquad otherwise.
                      \\end{cases}
              %p In the section on integration below we will see why this deserves the name “delta function”.
          %h2#the_cogerm_differential The cogerm differential
          %p
            For any curve
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi c
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
            and real number
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi h
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi c
                    %mi h
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c_h
            be the curve defined by
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi c
                      %mi h
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi t
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi t
                    %mo +
                    %mi h
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c_h(t) = c(t+h)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ω
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
            is any cogerm differential 1-form, then we define its
            %strong differential
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} d
                  %mi ω
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{d}\omega
            by
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} d
                  %mi ω
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mi c
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %mo =
                  %munder
                    %mi lim
                    %mrow
                      %mi h
                      %mo →
                      %mn 0
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                      %mi ω
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %msub
                        %mi c
                        %mi h
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                      %mo −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                      %mi ω
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi c
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                    %mi h
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \langle \mathrm{d}\omega | c \rangle = \lim_{h\to 0} \frac{\langle \omega | c_h \rangle - \langle \omega | c\rangle}{h}.
          %p
            Note that while the fraction on the right-hand side only makes sense for a specific representative curve
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi c
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
            and a sufficiently small
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi h
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
          %p
            Of course, in general,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} d
                  %mi ω
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{d}\omega
            may not be defined on as many curves as
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ω
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
            is.
          .un_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is a smooth space, so that we have a notion of
              = succeed "," do
                %em smooth curve
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
              is
              %strong smooth
              if
            %ol
              %li
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ω
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
                is defined on all germs of smooth curves, and
              %li
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} d
                      %mi ω
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{d}\omega
                is smooth (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coinductive+definition"}> coinductively
                ).
          %p
            For example, if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi ℝ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:X\to \mathbb{R}
            is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+function"} smooth function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} d
                    %mi n
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{d}^n f
            are those mentioned above. By stopping the coinduction at an appropriate point and requiring only
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+function"} continuity
            = succeed "-times" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuously+differentiable+function"} continuously differentiable function
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^k
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ω
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
            is
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^2
            if
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} d
                    %mi ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{d}\omega
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} d
                    %mn 2
                  %mi ω
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{d}^2\omega
            are defined on all smooth curves and the last of these is continuous. (But the obvious definition of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differentiable+function"} differentiable function
            without continuity is too weak, even if we require
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} d
                  %mi ω
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{d}\omega
            to be defined on all differentiable germs, as the classic example of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %msup
                    %mi y
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi x
                    %mn 2
                  %mo +
                  %msup
                    %mi y
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x y^2/(x^2 + y^2)
            shows; extended continuously to the origin, this and its differential are defined on all smooth curves, although the differential is not continuous, but this function is not differentiable, which we know because its differential is not linear as a covector form.)
          %p
            Note that the cogerm differential
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} d
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{d}
            is
            %em not
            the same as the exterior differential, except when applied to
            = succeed "-forms." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} d
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ≠
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{d}^2 \neq 0
          %p We have the expected multivariable chain rule:
          .un_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo :
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo →
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi:\mathbb{R}^n\to \mathbb{R}
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differentiable+function"} differentiable function
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ω
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi ω
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega_1,\dots,\omega_n
              are cogerm differential 1-forms, then
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi ω
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi ω
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mo ∂
                      %mn 1
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi ω
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi ω
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} d
                    %msub
                      %mi ω
                      %mn 1
                    %mo +
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo +
                    %msub
                      %mo ∂
                      %mi n
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi ω
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi ω
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} d
                    %msub
                      %mi ω
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{d}(\phi(\omega_1,\dots,\omega_n)) = \partial_1\phi(\omega_1,\dots,\omega_n) \mathrm{d}\omega_1 + \cdots +  \partial_n\phi(\omega_1,\dots,\omega_n) \mathrm{d}\omega_n
            %p
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo ∂
                      %mi i
                    %mi ϕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \partial_i\phi
              denotes the partial derivative with respect to the
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi i
                      %mi th
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i^{th}
              variable.
          %p
            In particular, taking
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi x
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi(x,y) = x y
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} d
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ω
                  %mi η
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi ω
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} d
                  %mi η
                  %mo +
                  %mi η
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} d
                  %mi ω
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{d}(\omega\eta) = \omega \mathrm{d}\eta + \eta \mathrm{d}\omega.
          %p
            This also enables us to calculate the iterated cogerm differentials of functions. If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi ℝ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x:X\to \mathbb{R}
            is a “coordinate” and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi ℝ
                  %mo →
                  %mi ℝ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:\mathbb{R}\to \mathbb{R}
            is a function, so that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi ℝ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(x) : X\to \mathbb{R}
            is a function of that coordinate, then by the theorem we have
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} d
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi f
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} d
                  %mi x
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{d}f(x) = f'(x) \mathrm{d}x.
          %p Thus, by the product rule, we have
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} d
                    %mn 2
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi f
                  %mo ″
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} d
                  %msup
                    %mi x
                    %mn 2
                  %mo +
                  %mi f
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msup
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} d
                    %mn 2
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{d}^2 f(x) = f''(x) \mathrm{d}x^2 + f'(x) \mathrm{d}^2x
          %p
            and so on. Note that the first formula justifies the common notation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} d
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} d
                      %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{\mathrm{d}f(x)}{\mathrm{d}x}
            for the derivative
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f'(x)
            %em almost
            justifies the common notation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} d
                        %mn 2
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} d
                      %msup
                        %mi x
                        %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{\mathrm{d}^2f(x)}{\mathrm{d}x^2}
            for the second derivative
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo ″
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f''(x)
            — it would be correct only if
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} d
                      %mn 2
                    %mi x
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{d}^2x=0
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo ″
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mfrac
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mo ∂
                          %mn 2
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mo ∂
                        %msup
                          %mi x
                          %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f''(x) = \frac{\partial^2f(x)}{\partial x^2}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo ″
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f''(x)
            is the coefficient of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} d
                  %msup
                    %mi x
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{d}x^2
            in a canonical expansion of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} d
                      %mn 2
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{d}^2 f(x)
          %h2#integration Integration
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi c
                  %mo :
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c:[a,b] \to X
            be a curve and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ω
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
            a cogerm differential 1-form; we would like to integrate
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ω
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
            over
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
          %h3#naive_integration Naive integration
          %p
            The
            %strong naive integral
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ω
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
            over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi c
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
            is defined to be
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo ∫
                    %mi c
                  %mi ω
                  %mo =
                  %msubsup
                    %mo ∫
                    %mrow
                      %mi t
                      %mo =
                      %mi a
                    %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                  %mi ω
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %msub
                    %mi c
                    %mi t
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} d
                  %mi t
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \int_c \omega = \int_{t=a}^b \langle \omega | c_t \rangle \mathrm{d}t.
          %p
            if this exists. If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ω
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
            is an exterior differential
            = succeed "-form" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
            = succeed "-form," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
          %h3#genuine_integration Genuine integration
          %p
            The
            %strong (genuine) integral
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ω
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
            over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi c
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
            is defined as follows. Given a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tagged+partition"} tagged partition
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi t
                    %mn 0
                  %mo &lt;
                  %msub
                    %mi t
                    %mn 1
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo &lt;
                  %msub
                    %mi t
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo &lt;
                  %msub
                    %mi t
                    %mi n
                  %mo =
                  %mi b
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a = t_0 \lt t_1 \cdots \lt t_{n-1} \lt t_n = b
            with tags
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi t
                      %mi i
                      %mo *
                    %mo ∈
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msub
                      %mi t
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi t
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
