                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} d
                    %mn 2
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{d}^2x
            are “second-order” quantities and hence ought to be negligible. For instance, we usually compute the area under a curve
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi y
                  %mo =
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y=f(x)
            between
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo =
                  %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x=a
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
