          %h3#parametrization_invariance Parametrization invariance
          %p Since both naive and genuine integrals agree with ordinary line integrals when restricted to exterior 1-forms, such integrals are invariant under orientation-preserving reparametrization. However, for general cogerm 1-forms, neither integral is so invariant. Nevertheless, we may ask for conditions under which they are.
          %p
            The naive integral is very much not invariant under reparametrization. This is most obvious when
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ω
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
            is just a function, in which case its integral is just its ordinary integral. Similarly, a naive integral like
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo ∫
                      %mi c
                    %msup
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} d
                      %mn 2
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \int_c \mathrm{d}^2 x
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
