                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi o
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi dx
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} o(dx)
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi c
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
                might be, any such integral is parametrization-independent.
            %li
              %p
                The genuine integral of any form along any curve is invariant under orientation-preserving
                %em affine
                reparametrization. This follows fairly directly from its definition.
          %p
            There are forms whose genuine integral exists, but is not parametrization-invariant, such as
            = succeed "." do
